{"name":"Clotted Cream","hex":"#f3efcd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"clotted cream","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A thick, sweet dairy product, made by skimming the thickened layer off the top of unhomogenized cream that has been heated and allowed to stand. Fat content is at least 55%."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clotted_cream"}],"entries":[{"title":"Clotted cream","blocks":[{"text":"Clotted cream is a thick cream made by heating full-cream cow's milk using steam or a water bath and then leaving it in shallow pans to cool slowly. During this time, the cream content rises to the surface and forms \"clots\" or \"clouts\", hence the name. Clotted cream is an essential ingredient for cream tea."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Clotted_cream_%28cropped%29.JPG/330px-Clotted_cream_%28cropped%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clotted_cream","wikidata":"Q1373885"},{"title":"Cream","blocks":[{"text":"Cream is a dairy product composed of the higher-fat layer skimmed from the top of milk before homogenization. The butterfat, which is less dense, rises to the top and is skimmed off, resulting in gravity cream. The industrial production of cream instead uses centrifugal separators to make separator cream. Cream is often sold in grades defined by their butterfat content. It contains high levels of saturated fat, in ascending proportion from light cream to heavy cream."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/01_Mmm..._Apple_Crisp_with_Whipped_Cream.jpg/330px-01_Mmm..._Apple_Crisp_with_Whipped_Cream.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cream","wikidata":"Q13228"},{"title":"Cream (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Cream is the color of the cream produced by cattle grazing on natural pasture with plants rich in yellow carotenoid pigments, some of which are incorporated into the fresh milk. This gives a yellow tone to otherwise-white milk at higher fat concentrations. Cream is the pastel colour of yellow, much as pink is to red. By mixing yellow and white, cream can be produced."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Milk_heavy_cream_B.jpg/330px-Milk_heavy_cream_B.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cream_(colour)","wikidata":"Q2730433"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Carn_Euny_fogou_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1297253.jpg/500px-Carn_Euny_fogou_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1297253.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Carn_Euny_fogou_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1297253.jpg/500px-Carn_Euny_fogou_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1297253.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Roman-era Cornish fogou or souterrain","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACarn_Euny_fogou_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1297253.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Parsonage_Farm-_Dairy_Farming_in_Devon%2C_England%2C_1942_D10226.jpg/500px-Parsonage_Farm-_Dairy_Farming_in_Devon%2C_England%2C_1942_D10226.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Parsonage_Farm-_Dairy_Farming_in_Devon%2C_England%2C_1942_D10226.jpg/500px-Parsonage_Farm-_Dairy_Farming_in_Devon%2C_England%2C_1942_D10226.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" A 'Cow Man' weighs milk at Dartington, 1942.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AParsonage_Farm-_Dairy_Farming_in_Devon%2C_England%2C_1942_D10226.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Clotted_cream_tin.jpg/50